Package: drivesync
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kwallet6 | gnome-keyring
Description: Synchronize chosen folders with Google Drive
 DriveSync connects Google accounts and keeps folders you choose on this
 computer in step with folders on Google Drive: uploads, downloads, renames
 and moves, with conflicts kept for you to decide and permanent deletion
 never used. Credentials are kept by the desktop's Secret Service (KDE
 Wallet or GNOME Keyring), never in a file.
 .
 This build shows DriveSync in Plasma's system tray, reports completed,
 failed and conflicting synchronization as Plasma notifications, adds the
 synchronized folder to Dolphin's Places when asked, and holds
 synchronization while the connection is metered. Its interface is in the
 edition's ten languages.
 .
 Built from the source of one commit of DriveSync's development branch with
 its Rust crates vendored, not from upstream's Flatpak. DriveSync is an early
 technical preview by its author.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Pawel "pavroo"
 Pijanowski). Upstream: Rafael Tosta.
